{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The alef of ויקרא is small — Moses did not want to write anything but ויקר, as it is written regarding Balaam, as if HaShem only appeared to him by chance. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: write also with an alef, and he wrote it small. ויקרא אל משה — rashei tevot: אמ\"ו — his mother crowned him. Moses preceded [the name of] HaShem, as it were, like one who speaks with his friend and precedes him out of courtesy. It is written above: ואש תהיה לילה בו, and adjacent to it: ויקרא אל משה — meaning, since He called to him and spoke with him, his face burned like fire." "<b> בכל מסעיהם ויקרא אל משה</b> — meaning, in all their journeys He called to Moses [saying] they should journey, as it is written: ע\"פ ה' יסעו. Five alefs in the verse, corresponding to the five books of the Torah. And there are nine words in it, and likewise there are nine words in the paragraph אנכי ה' אלהיך — meaning, anyone who studies Torah is as if he offered all the sacrifices. And likewise nine words in the verse זאת התורה לעולה."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:49.398021361Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}